charlie wrote:
> I just reached the boulders and pits levels last night.

That's the Sokoban branch, incidentally. ;)

> I was wondering if I can get rid of the jumpy feeling.

I don't know how much you want to be spoiled, so I'll be vague for now.
There is a creature which can remove any and all intrinsics, at random,
and only during certain hours. If you decide to go that route, be
prepared to lose most of your good intrinsics in the process. You can
get them back, but it's still a huge PITA. However, to the best of my
knowledge, it is the *only* way to lose that particular intrinsic
entirely.

> Does it time out or do I have to hope that I can find a
> controlling item before I die stupidly?

Once you have teleportitis, you're pretty well stuck with it, except
for the one possibility I alluded to. There are ways of gaining
teleport control that don't involve magical items, however. As a hint,
do you know of any creatures in the dungeon that seem to share your
affliction? In any event, if you can gain teleport control,
teleportitis can actually be pretty handy. It doesn't always kick in
when you need it to, but if you play a character that doesn't stand a
snowball's chance in Gehennom of succesfully casting a teleport spell,
it's better than nothing.

> I had played "Castle of the Winds" (basically a comercial
