Oh, wow. I thought I was the only person on the planet who had played
that game. I even used a resource editor to create a whole new tileset.
Although I never knew it at the time (I didn't encounter NetHack until
a couple years ago), NetHack had to have been the inspiration for that
game. I guess it could have been some other roguelike, but I strongly
suspect NetHack. I only played Diablo a few times, but I remember
wondering if they borrowed the "home scroll" idea from the "rune of
return" in Castle of the Winds.

> Oh and I'm finally learning to *slow down*.

That's probably the best general NetHack advice that anyone can give.
It's applicable at all levels of play. I've died by YASD in Gehennom
more times than I care to admit because I didn't follow that rule. You
get the point where your character is *almost* unstoppable, with
"almost" being the operative word. It's very easy, at that point, to
start racing through the game without really thinking hard about what
you're doing.



